<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John of Neuilly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1220</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John of Neuilly was a Frankish knight and hereditary marshal of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>. Around 1220 he received a fief at the entrance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> peninsula in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> and built the castle of Passavant to control the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maniots">Maniots</a>. His family held the barony until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> recovered the area in the 1260s.</p></div>
